' keeper autostart example -- keep this file ASCII-only!
' (wscript reads .vbs without BOM as ANSI; non-ASCII comments can break it)
' 1. Fix the two paths below (pythonw.exe and keeper.py).
' 2. Rename to keeper.vbs and drop it in your Startup folder (Win+R -> shell:startup).
' 3. Log out/in, or run it once to start the keeper right away.
CreateObject("WScript.Shell").Run """C:\path\to\pythonw.exe"" ""C:\path\to\keeper.py""", 0, False
